# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY and not a
# SYMLINK, so a symlinked node_modules slips past it and can be committed — which
# is how a self-referential `node_modules -> node_modules` reached main and
# replaced the installed packages in every checkout that pulled it. Bare
# `node_modules` matches both.
node_modules
dist/
.env
*.local
